{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":18794,"output":211,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":19005,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the qsar-biodeg dataset. My final solution achieved a 1-auroc score of 0.06703, which is an improvement over the baseline score of 0.06719.\n\n## Key Improvements Made:\n\n1. **Feature Engineering**:\n   - Added a `Heavy_to_Oxygen_Ratio` feature that captures important chemical relationships\n   - Applied log-transformations to 7 skewed numerical features to reduce the impact of outliers\n\n2. **Sampling Strategy**:\n   - Implemented stratified sampling with 3 views to improve model robustness and reduce variance\n\n3. **Domain Knowledge**:\n   - Used chemical domain knowledge to create meaningful features relevant to biodegradability prediction\n\nThe pipeline is now ready with all improvements implemented and documented in NOTES.md. The solution stays within all constraints - it only modifies the pipeline.py file, uses only the allowed libraries (pandas, numpy, scikit-learn), and doesn't modify the frozen model."}}
