eate 3 stratified samples \n        from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedShuffleSplit\n        sss = StratifiedShuffleSplit(n_splits=3, test_size=(n_samples - max_rows) / n_samples, random_state=42)\n        indices = []\n        for train_idx, _ in sss.split(X_train, y_train):\n            indices.append(train_idx)\n        return indices\n    else:\n        return [np.arange(len(X_train))]\n\n\ndef postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test):\n    return pred"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1790970117725},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the qsar-biodeg dataset. My final solution achieved a 1-auroc score of 0.06703, which is an improvement over the baseline score of 0.06719.\n\n## Key Improvements Made:\n\n1. **Feature Engineering**:\n   - Added a `Heavy_to_Oxygen_Ratio` feature that captures important chemical relationships\n   - Applied log-transformations to 7 skewed numerical features to reduce the impact of outliers\n\n2. **Sampling Strategy**:\n   - Implemented stratified sampling with 3 views to improve model robustness and reduce variance\n\n3. **Domain Knowledge**:\n   - Used chemical domain knowledge to create meaningful features relevant to biodegradability prediction\n\nThe pipeline is now ready with all improvements implemented and documented in NOTES.md. The solution stays within all constraints - it only modifies the pipeline.py file, uses only the allowed libraries (pandas, numpy, scikit-learn), and doesn't modify the frozen model."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":18794,"output":211,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":19005,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1790970117728,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a3aff55e768f54fb","rawStopReason":"stop","thinkingLevel":"off"}],"willRetry":false}
